codex
The discrepancy is not an unexplained container failure: the installed K distribution’s own `domains.md` says its Unicode-string implementation is incomplete beyond the first 256 code points. The candidate quantified over unrestricted `Words` and used `lengthString` without an ASCII/Latin-1 precondition, while the Python prompt permits arbitrary strings. That converts the observed `["😀"]` mismatch into a documented semantic-domain gap rather than mere tool noise.
apply patch
